content:
maya: Observed duplicate POSTs from the Android SDK in production traces when a coroutine gets cancelled and our retry logic fires. Repro fairly reliable on emulator with network slowness.

sam: hmm. Are you doing manual retries or relying on OkHttp? POST should be non-retriable by default in most conservative configs.

maya: We added a small retry helper in the SDK because carriers sometimes drop connections. It catches IOExceptions and does call.clone().execute(). Works for a while but with coroutine cancellations it replays. Example repro attached below.

lucas: can you paste the minimal repro snippet? Also which OkHttp + kotlin coroutines versions?

maya: OkHttp 4.11.0, kotlin-coroutines 1.7.3. Snippet:```kotlin
suspend fun submitOrder(body: RequestBody): Response = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
  val req = Request.Builder().url("${BASE}/orders").post(body).build()
  val call = client.newCall(req)
  try {
    return@withContext call.execute()
  } catch (e: IOException) {
    // naive retry
    return@withContext call.clone().execute()
  }
}
```

qa-ana: what's the cancellation vector? UI pressing back, or scope.cancel()?

maya: We cancel the coroutine scope when the Activity goes to background + also have a manual cancel button in the sample. If the coroutine is cancelled while socket is stalled, the catch block still runs and clones the call. clone() does not inherit cancellation so server sees second POST.

sam: got it. Short term: do not retry non-idempotent methods unless an Idempotency-Key header exists. Also check coroutineContext.isActive before retrying.

lucas: better long term: use suspendCancellableCoroutine + enqueue so cancellation propagates to the active call. Pattern:```kotlin
suspend fun Call.awaitResponse(): Response = suspendCancellableCoroutine { cont ->
  enqueue(object : Callback {
    override fun onResponse(c: Call, r: Response) { if (!cont.isCancelled) cont.resume(r) }
    override fun onFailure(c: Call, e: IOException) { if (!cont.isCancelled) cont.resumeWithException(e) }
  })
  cont.invokeOnCancellation { cancel() }
}
```

maya: that's cleaner. I also noticed our RetryInterceptor swallows InterruptedIOException and still retries; maybe OkHttp changed behavior in 4.11 where timeouts throw different subclass.

qa-ana: can we add a CI test that runs the sample app in emulator with network shaping (adb shell network delay) and triggers rapid cancellation to assert server saw only one POST? We can feed the test to infra job.

sam: yeah add a gcloud emu job that runs 500 iterations and asserts no duplicates. Also add a small integration harness on staging that returns idempotency-mismatch logs so QA can detect dupes.

maya: I'll update SDK: 1) switch to cancellable enqueue wrapper 2) only retry POST when header "Idempotency-Key" present 3) add telemetry event when clone() used so we can detect live anomalies. Will open PR.

dev-bot: created QA build 334 with cancellable wrapper + idempotency guard. Rolling to emulator pool.

qa-ana: will run 1000 fuzz runs and paste summary here. If pass rate < 99.9% I'll file a follow-up.

sam: also note in release notes: behavior change for retry semantics on POSTs — call out to customers.

maya: thanks all. PR incoming with unit + emulator integration test. Will include a tiny sample app for reproducing locally (link in PR).
